body:
## 2026-09-07 economy decision and tuning acceptance
Recent earn/spend and +1 EXTRA LANE PRESSURE feedback already landed; preserve it and test its actual consequence before adding more labels.

Record a short normal-match baseline: first affordable decision, source of gold, purchase opportunities, creep pressure before/after spend and time until a win/loss opportunity. Compare extra-unit versus upgrade choice at matched initial state; exact tuning remains data-driven. Do not claim balance from UI wording.

Reject duplicate/stale/invalid purchase requests, insufficient gold, terminal-match spending and disconnected-client attempts through the existing authoritative transaction path. Spend and resulting unit/upgrade happen exactly once; rematch resets only declared match state.

Keep earthworks free and map-wide as required by the northstar; do not attach the construction/shop economy to terrain editing. Construction cost and salvage/refund remain their own declared rules.

Use the existing shop/economy/HUD owners. P3TowerDefenseFeatureActor.cpp and P3LaneWarHUDWidget.cpp serialize with #2437/#2440 and other current contributors. Evidence/tuning analysis can proceed without editing those files.

---

Parent: #803 / #941.

Turn the existing Lane War economy into a player decision loop. Reuse current gold, creep-shop and upgrade authority; no new economy framework.

Acceptance:
- gold rises from the intended creep-related play and periodic income;
- the player can clearly see current gold and what can be bought;
- buying an extra allied creep/minion visibly changes lane pressure;
- buying a creep upgrade visibly changes later allied creeps and communicates the new level/effect;
- pacing is playable enough that a normal short match demonstrates earn -> choose -> spend -> visible consequence;
- server authority/replication remain the existing implementation.
